The iOS build lands here.

ci/app/deliver-ios.sh writes strong-fish-v<VERSION>.ipa into this directory on a
Mac, and it is committed - the Linux pipeline cannot build one but does have to
serve it, so the file crosses between them through git.

This placeholder keeps the directory in the repository, which is what lets the
Dockerfile copy the directory unconditionally: COPY fails on a glob that
matches nothing, so "the .ipa if there is one" has to be spelled as "this
directory, whatever is in it".
